      "writtenOn": "2022-06-23T17:29:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Testing this with make try_build_boards, it looks like we need to use ifdef to prevent an implicit declaration error if the function is declared behind a config. But if the function is declared and not defined, either ifdef of IS_ENABLED will work to prevent an undefined reference error.\n\nIn this case, chipset_power_on is declared in chipset.h but only if CONFIG_AP_POWER_CONTROL is defined. So, we need to use ifdef to check that CONFIG_AP_POWER_CONTROL is defined before calling it. It is defined in power_button_x86.c and qcom.c, so IS_ENABLED will work for the rest of the conditions here to make sure we don\u0027t call it if it\u0027s declared but never defined.",
      "parentUuid": "fdfe86de_bf1b5b18",
      "revId": "adf183b3422b5470f5dd38e219b67252950a05e5",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
