      "writtenOn": "2022-06-23T17:29:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is a remnant from an earlier version of this CL (patchset 4) which included shutting down the AP on long button presses. Then, it was right before a long button press so it was to show that while the device was awake, a short button press doesn\u0027t do anything but a long button press will shutdown the AP.\n\nI left it in after removing AP shutdown to show that short presses will do nothing when the device is awake, but wake the device when it is in G3/S5. But, you\u0027re right that now the comment is misleading.\n\nTo answer your question - nothing should happen because the AP is already on. I changed the comment accordingly.\n\nAlso, I added another press to this test so now there are 3. (1) valid press while AP is on - nothing should happen. (2) Invalid press while AP is off - nothing should happen. (3) Valid press while AP is off - device should wake.",
